261	 * security reviewer. No repository-configured command runs while it is built (see GIT_SAFE and safeGitEnv); a
262	 * filter or diff driver that would still apply makes it fail. It is built from the changed paths and never from parsing diff text: the changed paths come from
263	 * NUL-separated git output with rendering options pinned, the protected ones (the read_file policy, `.nexus`) are
264	 * removed, and the diff is then requested for the remaining paths only (literal pathspecs), so a protected file cannot
265	 * appear in it whatever the repository's diff settings. A rename or copy with either side protected drops both sides
266	 * (the body of a file renamed out of a protected path is still its content).
